Modifications by the streetCryptid project
------------------------------------------

2026-11-01 — Pending path opens are queued once per address:

  * src/socket/remote_map/remote_state.rs
      - `open_path_on_conn` pushes an address onto `pending_open_paths` only if it is
        not already there. Upstream pushed it once per connection that refused the open
        (RemoteCidsExhausted / MaxPathIdReached), and the 333 ms retry replays the whole
        queue over every connection, so the queue multiplied by the connection count on
        every retry. An iPhone with a dozen connections to a nearby Pixel aborted in
        `VecDeque::grow` (allocation failure) about a second into a Bump.

The crate's Cargo.lock and .cargo_vcs_info.json were not vendored. No other file differs
from the published 1.0.2 crate.
